How to run the API:
1. Open your virtual Machine.
2. Input the collowing commands one by one on your PowerShell

sudo systemctl stop iot-api            # frees port 8000 for the test
git clone https://github.com/zatguy79/ECSE3038-test2.git
cd ECSE3038-test2/api
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
nano .env              # Input your MONGODB_URI=...  and  MQTT_NAME=<name> here
uvicorn app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000

3. The app should now be running on your VM, enjoy!

How to run the board:

1. Download the board folder and place it in a suitable location.
2. Ensure you have the PlatformIO extension installed on your VSCode.
3. Open a new window in VSCode and click the anthead on the sidebar
4. Select "Pick a Folder" and open up the board folder
5. Create a include folder and place a secrets.h file in there and format it like this:

#ifndef SECRETS_H
#define SECRETS_H

#define WIFI_SSID "Wifi Network"
#define WIFI_PASSWORD "Wifi Network"
#define WIFI_CHANNEL number
#define X_API_KEY "Your API Key"
#define MQTT_NAME "Your MQTT Name"

#endif

6. Click the tick on the bottom to build and when it's done, press F1 to Start the Simulation by lcikcing "Wokwi: Start Simulator"
7. Enjoy!
